# Ignore rules at the git toplevel.
#
# The repository already carries .gitignore files under Aurora-Motor-Engine/ and
# hybrid-agent-fabric/, but nothing at the top level — which is what the release
# hygiene ratchet (T1) checks, and what `git add .` from a fresh clone consults
# first. Without it, the first build run from the repository root was one
# `git add .` away from committing node_modules and dist into history.

# Dependencies and build output
node_modules/
dist/
build/
out/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Environment and local secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key

# Coverage and tooling caches
coverage/
.cache/
.parcel-cache/
.vite/
.turbo/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*

# Editor and OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
*.swp

# Runtime state that used to be tracked and no longer is (116 files removed
# from the index).
#
#   .config/Electron/          114 committed files of Chromium cache, code cache
#                              and Crashpad dumps — per-machine state that can
#                              never merge cleanly.
#   .sudo_as_admin_successful  a zero-byte sandbox marker.
#   /package-lock.json         a stray "name": "user" lockfile with an empty
#                              packages map. The real workspace root is
#                              Aurora-Motor-Engine/hybrid-agent-fabric, which
#                              carries its own lockfile.
#
# None of the three is referenced by any code, test, script or CI workflow.
# They remain in git history; removing them from history needs a rewrite, which
# is deliberately not done here.
.config/Electron/
.sudo_as_admin_successful
/package-lock.json

# NOT ignored: `uploads/` holds AURORA_NIHAI_MASTER_YOL_HARITASI.md, a real
# 39 KB design document. Runtime uploads go to `.haf/uploads/` instead
# (main.ts:2057), so the tracked directory is documentation, not staging.
